sion + config captured\n- [ ] QINSy project template for BizzyBoat (reference frames, sensor list, outputs)\n- [ ] Identify SVS model from serial stream (suspected AML)\n- [ ] COM port assignments recorded in log\n\n### NTRIP strategy investigation\nSBG antennas are independent of the Cube's RTK chain. Decide between:\n- [ ] SBG uses its own NTRIP client direct from MACORS\n- [ ] Share MACORS credentials / split corrections\n- [ ] Route corrections via mercat to SBG serial\n\nDocument rationale + implement chosen path.\n\n### Calibration planning\n- [ ] Bench shakedown procedure (shore power, all devices live)\n- [ ] Patch test plan (roll/pitch/yaw/latency on water)\n- [ ] SVP procedure — SVS feed into QINSy; cast vs. continuous decision\n\n### Documentation\n- [ ] Detailed install log at `bizzyboat_project11/docs/hydro_payload_install_log.md` kept current\n- [ ] Summary entries in `bizzyboat_deployment_log.md` per session\n- [ ] Update `project_kongsberg_m3.md` memory (protocol confirmed)\n- [ ] Update `project_bizzyboat_autonomy_stack.md` memory (payload added)\n\n## Success criteria\n\n1. All sensors powered, communicating, and logged on mercat\n2. NTRIP strategy chosen and corrections flowing to SBG\n3. QINSy produces bathymetric soundings referenced to SBG nav\n4. Patch test + SVP procedures documented\n5. mercat timing is traceable (NTP synced to known source)\n\nPart of #57\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}